# G3 (SOFT, a ONE-JOB chain, READ FIRST: a human stop, not the driver's). IMAGE: tp4-stack-1 (the broken stack; exists on the rig). The integrated stack on the gate profile, warmup +
# concurrent4_steady ONLY, from a fresh container: all four steady prefills run BEFORE the first packed round, so this cannot trigger
# the trigger (a prefill after a packed replay) and tests the steady prompts' prefill and the pair path on a clean target.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over the job file on a throwaway
# commit of tp4/stack-fix (or a descendant) and push the window tag. Nothing here names a rig, a card or a registry. The smoke and its
# check run from the CHECKOUT on the rig host; the server is the IMAGE'S baked tree (--read-only, no bind mount), so C2_IMAGE_TAG picks
# the server and the checkout picks the smoke and the check. THE DRIVER SUBSTITUTES C2_IMAGE_TAG FROM ITS IMAGE_TAG ENV: a chain that
# sets one IMAGE_TAG for all its jobs runs every job on that image, so jobs that need different images are SEPARATE ONE-JOB CHAINS.
# PREDICTION (families A or B, the diagnosis): four coherent answers, '[PACKED-SELECT] round=N pairs=[[0, 1], [2, 3]] users=4' lines.
# EOS or garbage from a user's FIRST token here refutes both and points at the steady prompts' prefill layout; breakage only after the
# pairs engage points at tp4/draft. The stack image lacks the fix, so the checkout's first-prefill ledger rule WILL print 'the first
# prefill left N model buffers' and the run WILL end red whatever the text: that line is the image's known late allocation, not a G3
# verdict; judge by smoke.log and the container timeline. Read: per-user tokens/finish/text; 'Prefilling 1 user(s) into slots';
# 'pair row exact engaged'. Duration (estimate): 6-9 min (K1, a four-test smoke on the same image family: 6.3 min).
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-stack-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-gate
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,concurrent4_steady
